    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>&#160;vs&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>&nbsp;plot for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;orbital of single-electron species will be</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a950eb3b-9630-469b-b5a3-4fd5b7183842-9712446_B.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 187px;\" /></p><p>Here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;represent probability density of finding an electron wave at a position around nucleus. The 2s orbital will also have a nodal plane.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
